  <ym-title|Bounded refresh of the OPE closure
  interfaces><label|bounded-refresh-of-the-ope-closure-interfaces>

  Parent audit, 12 November 2026. Source pin
  <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>. This records current
  manuscript interfaces and existing correspondence leads. It is not a new
  proof, a source absence finding, or an independent OPE review.

  <section|Why another OPE derivation is not the next
  task><label|why-another-ope-derivation-is-not-the-next-task>

  The current text already contains the finite prescription, homogeneous
  averaging, local grouping/transfer, cutoff matching accounting, physical
  filtration, all-character price transfer, grid interpolation and final
  raw-to-homogeneous estimate arguments. Several older paragraphs still
  describe downstream inputs as unproved. Do not infer a new missing theorem
  merely from that wording; check the newer canonical producers. Conversely,
  the presence of both chapters does not establish that their hypotheses
  agree on one selected history.

  <section|Exact interfaces to reconcile in
  C05><label|exact-interfaces-to-reconcile-in-c05>

  <\enumerate>
    <item><verbatim|ope-grid.tex>, <verbatim|input:ope-match>, needs ONE
    sequence of original degree-q labels Q_n with discrepancy price rate
    tau(p;a,d)-(q+1/16)(a-b), quota-price rate tau(p;a,d)-qa, whole-label
    norm multiplier of rate qa, and low-filtration approximants at every
    1\<less\>=m\<less\>=q with relative norm rate (q-m)a. This is for every
    fixed differentiated cluster list and
    0\<less\>b\<less\>a\<less\>x\<less\>d; positions and phases may vary. It
    is not sufficient to choose a different Q_n for each phase or low degree.

    <item><verbatim|ope-cutoff.tex> constructs the rates, intermediate
    geometry and a same-match sublimit. Its displayed affordability
    conditions <verbatim|eq:ope-match-pay-one> and
    <verbatim|eq:ope-match-pay-two> precede the centered discrepancy bound
    <verbatim|eq:ope-cutoff-discrepancy>. The latter's finite-cutoff
    comparison is supplied mathematically by <verbatim|reference-match.tex>
    at its explicit signed-path, marked-transfer, chamber and
    terminal-reference inputs. Match the opening/matching index conventions
    explicitly: the reference chapter uses m for the opening and k for the
    match, whereas the OPE accounting uses k for the centered test and its
    opened K(k) for the opening, and m for the match. Check the actual
    one-step coefficient location and constants instead of substituting
    symbols by eye. The +5 complete-replicated-moment price is essential
    here.

    <item><verbatim|leaf-transfer.tex>, <verbatim|eq:leaf-projection-allowance>,
    gives the elementary coefficient/remainder and exact marked-profile
    identity needed by <verbatim|ope-local-projection.tex>,
    <verbatim|eq:ope-leaf-projection>. Its numerical conclusion is not a
    substitute for the stated raw derivative and profile hypotheses.
    <verbatim|ope-history-service.tex> supplies the selected-history
    compatibility and exact compression prices; C06/C08/C12/C16 must
    acknowledge the analytic supplier and the same adjacent transition at the
    exact parameters.

    <item><verbatim|ope-phase-prices.tex> proves the all-character transfer
    of the COMPLETE discrepancy on the same label sublimit, using centered
    prices and even moments. It also gives the rough cluster rate x*w(p) and
    the rate-zero fixed-clearance spectator insertions needed by the grid
    argument. It does not produce the finite-cutoff match, and it must use
    the same Q_n as item1.

    <item><verbatim|ope-filtration.tex>, <verbatim|eq:ope-physical-distance>,
    is the physical, not merely bare-coordinate, low-degree conclusion. Its
    normalized-test argument retains actual triangular transport, local
    protected-trial comparison and projections p_c-\<gtr\>p with vanishing
    tests on ker(p_c). <verbatim|finite-rank-kernel-transport.tex> explicitly
    points to this consumer, conditionally on its common projections. C14
    owns the finite-rank transport and equation/insertion relays; C13 owns
    the local-trial/selected-history estimates. Both packages must match them
    to these exact projections, cutoff-dependent derivative orders and
    thresholds. Fixed-order bounds or separate choices of sublimits do not
    suffice.

    <item>With items1\U5 established, <verbatim|ope-grid.tex> already proves
    the grid-to-all-point and derivative interpolation, and the
    intermediate-scale slack argument gives
    <verbatim|input:ope-raw-estimates>. <verbatim|ope-estimates.tex> then
    proves the homogeneous coefficient and full remainder bounds, including
    uniformity in varying geometry/phases by a violating-sequence argument.
    Preserve the finite truncation quantifiers and identity/empty-cluster
    cases.
  </enumerate>

  The matching and all-character discrepancy arguments use different
  refinements only where explicitly justified; the final matched label must
  retain all required bounds simultaneously. Cross-package acknowledgement
  should identify the exact producer labels, normalization, common
  family/filter and status, not just cite an entire section. The retained
  conditional statements must not be deleted until this ledger is actually
  discharged.

  <section|Canonical source leads (from existing
  correspondence)><label|canonical-source-leads-from-existing-correspondence>

  Consult <verbatim|ope-evidence.md>, <verbatim|ope-history-service-evidence.md>,
  <verbatim|ope-scale-purchases-evidence.md>, and the
  reference/local-projection evidence. These supply qualified declarations
  and inspected source records; their older status paragraphs may be
  superseded by current exact-hash reviews.

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|YM.OPE.funding>, <verbatim|YM.OPE.price_plot>,
    <verbatim|YM.OPE.height_room>: <verbatim|Lean/YM/OPE/Prices/{Circuit,Space}.lean>
    and the adjacent recorded sources.

    <item><verbatim|YM.OPE.Columns.limit_cap>, <verbatim|whole_origin>,
    <verbatim|fare_rate>, <verbatim|limit_lower>:
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/OPE/Columns/{Limit,Reannounce,ExtensionCost}.lean>.

    <item><verbatim|YM.OPE.found>, <verbatim|cloud_jump>,
    <verbatim|grid_coeff>, <verbatim|grid_remainder>,
    <verbatim|interpolated>, <verbatim|common_rate>, <verbatim|early_rate>:
    the exact Schemes/Interpolate/Eye paths recorded in
    <verbatim|ope-evidence.md>; resolve each declaration before making a
    fresh claim.

    <item>The selected service uses <verbatim|Campaign.opePackage17> and
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.exodusN> with the same purchased
    run; retain the final constant100 support profile rather than an
    illustrative alternative.
  </itemize-minus>

  This refresh did not independently reread those Lean declarations. It read
  the current TeX statements/proofs and the existing source correspondence,
  and used scoped <verbatim|rg> to locate the exact cross-references. No Lean
  build or axiom replay, no prose changes, and no new literature
  substitution. No claim that the list is an exhaustive OPE dependency graph.

